From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Tambe <tambewilliam@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:08:25 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] time: Add HZ_50

The ftpu, the RISC-V core of the FonTamSOC, has caches of one word per
line, direct mapped: between two ticks, the program which runs evicts
the code and the data of the tick, which every tick then reads again
from the DDR SDRAM, at tens of thousands of cycles. At 100 Hz, the
lowest choice, the tick thus takes a hart at 48 MHz some 14% of its
time, and more with several harts; NO_HZ_FULL, which depends on
HAVE_VIRT_CPU_ACCOUNTING_GEN, is out of reach of riscv32.

Add a choice of 50 Hz, which halves the timer interrupts. Its jiffy of
20 ms keeps a wait of the drivers of the SD card of the FonTamSOC, of
20 ms at most and rounded up to a jiffy, plus a tick, below the 100 ms
after which its devices abort a paused transmission.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: William Tambe <tambewilliam@gmail.com>
---
 kernel/Kconfig.hz | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/Kconfig.hz b/kernel/Kconfig.hz
index ce1435cb0..95baa647f 100644
--- a/kernel/Kconfig.hz
+++ b/kernel/Kconfig.hz
@@ -17,6 +17,12 @@ choice
 	 per second.
 
 
+	config HZ_50
+		bool "50 HZ"
+	help
+	  50 Hz halves the timer interrupts of 100 Hz, for systems whose
+	  timer interrupt is costly, at the expense of a coarser tick.
+
 	config HZ_100
 		bool "100 HZ"
 	help
@@ -50,6 +56,7 @@ endchoice
 
 config HZ
 	int
+	default 50 if HZ_50
 	default 100 if HZ_100
 	default 250 if HZ_250
 	default 300 if HZ_300
